# .gitignore — whitelist discipline
#
# Rationale: the Privacy Gradient (see the pattern doc) says private
# context never leaks upstream. A blacklist-shaped .gitignore fails
# open — a new secret-bearing file with an unanticipated extension
# slips through. A whitelist-shaped .gitignore fails closed — nothing
# is tracked unless explicitly permitted.
#
# The two lines below block everything by default, then whitelist the
# specific paths that belong in the Brain. Adjust the whitelist to
# match your Brain's actual layout; do NOT convert to blacklist-shape.

# Block everything by default
*

# Whitelist the Brain surface
!.gitignore
!.github/
!.github/**
!*.md
!AGENTS.md
!IDENTITY.md
!MEMORY.md
!SOUL.md
!USER.md
!memory/
!memory/**
!PROJECT_NOTES/
!PROJECT_NOTES/**
!scripts/
!scripts/**
!seed/
!seed/**
!tooling/
!tooling/**
!Makefile
!LICENSE
!README.md

# Block the classic secret-leaking classes even if whitelisted above
# (belt-and-braces; secret_scanner.py is the load-bearing gate)
**/.env
**/.env.*
**/*.pem
**/*.key
**/id_rsa
**/id_ed25519
**/.git-credentials
**/credentials
